    "title": "Control Board 5a: the logbook, and the night's fixes",
    "why": "decisions/0171 §10 (release 5, the session manager's OK): every switch, control, alarm and note in one logbook, newest first, filtered by system or process, with Log an entry. Folded in, from the night of 2026-11-19: a phase raises no alarm of its own (six trips repeated the workflows' own); a call carrying records is judged per record, so a big batch isn't slow; the unused check stops listing one- and two-letter columns; and Claude's held issue #19: a passing check closes a back-off issue, Check it now checks at once, and the system re-checks such an issue by itself hourly (never a refusal or block); and a server asking us to slow down (a 429, Wikidata's last night) is a warning that waits twice as long and clears itself, never a trip, with the watch turning any such trip back into a warning.",
